course: dictionary
lesson: 8978
title: One body, many workers
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A siphonophore is a sea animal that looks like one creature, but it is really a team. «A siphonophore looks like one long jellyfish but is a chain of many tiny animals living together, and some are longer than a blue whale.» The clues are "chain" and "living together", which tell you many small animals are joined up.
explain: Check your guess by swapping in a simpler idea. Try "a team of tiny animals joined together" in place of "a siphonophore". Does the sentence still make sense? If it does, your meaning is right.
explain: Notice that the sentence says it "looks like one" jellyfish. Things can look like one thing but be something different. That is a clue to read carefully.
fact: A siphonophore is a sea animal related to jellyfish.
fact: It is really a colony: many tiny animal parts joined together, working as one body.
fact: Each part has its own job: some swim, some catch food, some digest it, and some make young.
fact: The Portuguese man o' war is a famous siphonophore with stinging tentacles.
fact: Some deep-sea siphonophores are longer than a blue whale, though they are very thin.
exercise: What is a siphonophore? | *A colony of many tiny animal parts working as one | A single jellyfish with one body | A plant that grows on rocks | A fish with a hard shell
exercise: Some parts of a siphonophore swim and some catch food. What does this show? | All the parts do exactly the same job | The parts are rocks stuck together | Siphonophores cannot move at all | *Each part has its own job
exercise: Which word in «a chain of many tiny animals living together» tells you the animals are joined? | tiny | longer | *chain | animals
test: Some deep-sea siphonophores are «longer than a blue whale». What does this tell you? | They live on dry land | They are as small as a grain of sand | *They can be longer than a blue whale, though they are very thin | They are short and fat
test: Which animal is a famous siphonophore with stinging tentacles? | *The Portuguese man o' war | A blue whale | A starfish | A seahorse
exam: Using the clues in the lessons, what is a siphonophore best described as? | A jellyfish with one body | A rock on the sea floor | *A team of tiny animal parts living together as one animal | A kind of seaweed
